From a07dbd47d68ed99e6336051c812a6aea14b9511d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:24:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] agents.resume: continue a child from its own session
 transcript (agents.childSession)

Give every Pi child a Fabric-owned session file in its run directory so a
terminal run can be continued from the transcript it wrote, instead of
restarting from a text summary. The host records the exact launch beside the
run as the only thing a resume may re-execute; three manual resumes bound one
run. A resumed attempt runs on the plain pi runner, because pi-durable answers
from the result it recorded for the stored prompt.

Co-Authored-By: AI assistant
